          ":question/id": "72e836b6-2968-5b2e-8666-6c15080ad3e0",
          ":question/math-academy-id": "q-42005",
          ":question/problem": "Which of the following matrices are in row echelon form?\n\nSelect all that apply.",
          ":question/worked-solution": "Remember that a matrix is in row echelon form if it satisfies the following conditions:\n\n- All the zero rows (rows with only zeros), if any, are placed at the *bottom* of the matrix.\n- Each leading entry of a row is in a column *to the right* of the leading entry of the row above it.\n\nWith that in mind, let's look at each matrix in turn.\n\n- The matrix $A$ is not in row echelon form since ${a}_{32}\\ne 0$ (condition  II is violated). \n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 5 & 3 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 5 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 2 & 7 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n- The matrix $B$ is not in row echelon form since ${b}_{21}\\ne 0$ (condition II is violated). \n\n$$\nB=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 3 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -2 & 4 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 4 & -2 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n- The matrix $C$ is in row echelon form (both conditions are satisfied).\n\n$$\nC=\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 9 & 3 & 9 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 2 & 7 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 3\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nTherefore, only $C$ is in row echelon form."
        }
      ],
