              ":question/math-academy-id": "e-6166",
              ":question/problem": "What is the sum of the leading entries of the $1$st, $3$rd and $4$th rows in the matrix $A,$ given below?\n\n$$\nA=\n\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 1 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 7 & 8 \\\\ 0 & -4 & 2 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 8 & 4\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n",
              ":question/worked-solution": "The first non-zero entry of each row (from left to right) is the leading entry. \n\nTherefore, the leading entries of the $1$st, $3$rd and $4$th rows of $A$ are $-1$, $-4$ and $8$, respectively.\n\n$$\nA\n=\\begin{bmatrix}\\bbox[lightgray, 2pt]{-1} & 1 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 7 & 8 \\\\ 0 & \\bbox[lightgray, 2pt]{-4} & 2 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & \\bbox[lightgray, 2pt]{8} & 4\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nSo, the answer is $-1+(-4)+8=3.$"
