              ":tutorial/content": "Consider the following matrices:\n\n\n$$\nA = \\begin{bmatrix}2 & 6 & 7 & 8 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 6 & 9 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 4 & 7 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 5 & 8\\end{bmatrix}, \\qquad B = \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 5 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 4 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\n\n\nThe first non-zero entry on each row (from left to right) is called the **leading entry** of that row.\n\n- In the matrix $A,$ the leading entries are $a_{11}=2,$ $a_{22}=3,$ $a_{32}=1,$ and $a_{43}=5.$\n\n- In the matrix $B,$ the leading entries are $b_{11}=1,$ $b_{22}=3,$ $b_{33}=-2,$ and $b_{44}=2.$ The $5$th row has no leading entry.\n\nThe leading entries are highlighted below.\n\n\n\n$$\nA = \\begin{bmatrix}\\bbox[lightgray, 2pt]{2} & 6 & 7 & 8 \\\\ {\\color{blue}0} & \\bbox[lightgray, 2pt]{3} & 6 & 9 \\\\ {\\color{blue}0} & \\bbox[lightgray, 2pt]{{\\color{red}1}} & 4 & 7 \\\\ {\\color{blue}0} & {\\color{blue}0} & \\bbox[lightgray, 2pt]{5} & 8\\end{bmatrix}, \\qquad B = \\begin{bmatrix}\\bbox[lightgray, 2pt]{1} & 5 & 2 & 0 \\\\ {\\color{blue}0} & \\bbox[lightgray, 2pt]{3} & 4 & 3 \\\\ {\\color{blue}0} & {\\color{blue}0} & \\bbox[lightgray, 2pt]{-2} & 1 \\\\ {\\color{blue}0} & {\\color{blue}0} & {\\color{blue}0} & \\bbox[lightgray, 2pt]{2} \\\\ {\\color{blue}0} & {\\color{blue}0} & {\\color{blue}0} & {\\color{blue}0}\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n",
